<<~ aka "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/RFC-2119#/normative-language">>

<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The Invented Ripple

The Invented Ripple names a deferral justified by a migration cost the node never measured.

The refactor reads correct and the node names it as follow-up: //it would ripple through the CLI, the MCP surface, and the witnesses.// Measured afterward: ''three files, eight sites, and no MCP consumer existed at all.'' The ripple was invented, and it was invented in the same commit that named the invariant the deferral was violating.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ detect the moment a change gets named as follow-up rather than taken.
⏿ orient on WHY: name the cost out loud, in files and call-sites.
◇ decide by ''counting'', never by feel — `grep -rn` costs one call and answers exactly.
▶ act on the measurement: a small footprint takes the change now; a genuinely large one defers with the count recorded.
↺ if the count came back smaller than the story, mark it — the reflex that invented it will fire again.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

A deferral MUST carry a ''measured'' cost, never a narrated one.

The node MUST count the call-sites before naming a change as follow-up.
The node SHOULD record the count in the deferral itself, so a later hand reads the evidence rather than the story.
The node MAY defer on a large measured footprint; that reads as judgment rather than avoidance.

''What makes this specifically a CRAFT failure'': the invented cost always runs //larger// than the real one, and never smaller. The reflex protects the work already done — the shape of a diff, the passing tests — and dresses that protection as prudence about consumers who may not exist.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/diagnostic>>

If the node deferred and the measured footprint reads far smaller than the stated one, the Invented Ripple occurred.
If the node deferred with a count attached, judgment held.
If the node took the change and the footprint was genuinely large, that reads as a different failure — a scope breach, not this one.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

